What is the difference between welded flanges, flat welded flanges and socket welded flanges?
In HG, butt-welded flanges , flat-welded flanges and socket welded flanges have different standards. Applicable occasions are different, in addition, butt-welding flange is the pipe diameter and wall thickness of the interface end and the same as the pipe to be welded, and the two pipes are welded as well.
The welding performance of butt welding is better and the corrosion is smaller.
Flat welding is the same as butt welding with a boss, the boss is cut into a groove, and then the pipe is inserted into the welding.
Flat welding is slightly better than socket welding.
