High-purity sputtering target mainly refers to the purity of 99.9%-99.9999%(3N-6N Between ) Metal or non-metal target material, used in physical meteorological deposition of electronic components manufacturing (PVD) Process is the key material for preparing surface electronic films such as wafers, panels, solar cells, etc..Sputtering is one of the main techniques for preparing thin-film materials.
The bombarded solid is the raw material for the deposition of thin films by sputtering, which is called sputtering target..
Since 19 From the mid-century to the present, sputtering coating technology has experienced 170 Years of precipitation and development gradually mature.Sputtering coating technology originated from abroad, and the sputtering materials needed-the target material also originated and developed abroad.
A thin film with uniform thickness can be obtained on a large area of substrate material.
The advantages of strong binding force have become the main technology for preparing thin film materials.
According to different application areas, the material and shape of the target material will be different.According to the shape can be divided into long ( Positive ) Cuboid, cylindrical, random, solid and hollow targets can be divided into metal materials according to the material ( Pure metal aluminum / Titanium / Copper / Tantalum etc. )
Different materials and different shapes of targets need to be used in different applications
The barrier layer mainly has two functions.
The layer metal diffuses into the silicon, which is the main material of the wafer, and on the other hand, it is used as adhesion to bond the metal and the silicon material..Generally speaking, 110nm The wafers above the technology node use aluminum and titanium as the thin film materials of the wire and the barrier layer respectively.
Panel target: mainly used for production ITO Glass and touch screen electrode plate.The display industry mainly uses target sputtering coating in the production of display panels and touch screen panels, which are mainly used for production.
Photovoltaic targets: used to form the back electric level of thin-film solar cells.The target material is mainly used to generate the back electrode of the solar thin film battery, and the sputtering target material is rarely used in the crystalline silicon solar battery..Solar cells mainly include crystalline silicon solar cells and thin-film solar cells.
At present, the targets are mainly used in the field of solar thin-film cells.
99.99% Above.At present, the more commonly used sputtering targets for the preparation of solar cells include aluminum targets, copper targets, molybdenum targets, chromium targets and ITO Target, AZO Target ( Alumina zinc ) Wait.Among them, aluminum target and copper target are used for conductive layer film, molybdenum target and chromium target are used for barrier film, ITO Target, AZO Target for transparent conductive layer film.
The film system composed of the two can change the characteristics of light wave transmission, including light transmission, reflection, absorption, scattering, polarization and phase change.
Melting casting method and powder sintering method are the two main technical paths
Compared with the powder method, the impurity content (especially the gas impurity content) of the smelting alloy target is lower, and it can be high-density and large-scale.However, for several metals with large differences in melting point and density, it is generally difficult to obtain alloy targets with uniform composition by smelting methods..
Mainly used to prepare aluminum, copper, titanium, nickel-chromium alloy and other metals and alloy rotating targets with good plasticity.
From the perspective of the difficulty of the process, ultra-high purity metal control and purification technology, crystal grain orientation control technology, large-area welding technology of dissimilar metals, precision metal processing and special processing technology, and target cleaning and packaging technology are the current targets.
Quality.Among them, the crystal grain orientation control technology is mainly through the recrystallization process of plastic processing (TMP) That is, plastic processing-heat treatment-crystallization annealing to control the crystal orientation of the crystal grains, to make the size and arrangement direction of the crystal grains the same, to ensure the uniformity of sputtering film formation and sputtering speed, which is the core technology of target production.
→Two major steps: purification (preliminary purification), ultra-purification (final purification); →improving purity: chemical + physical purification
The crystal orientation of the crystal grains is usually controlled through the recrystallization process (TMP): plastic processing-heat treatment-crystallization annealing
Therefore, it is necessary to use different molding methods and heat treatment processes to control the crystalline orientation of the target according to the structural characteristics of the target..
