As we all know, the common methods used in vacuum coating are vacuum evaporation and merchant sputtering, so what is the difference between evaporation coating and sputtering coating?
Vacuum evaporation film is in the vacuum degree is not less than 10-2Pa environment, with resistance heating or electron beam and laser bombardment and other methods to evaporate the material heated to a fixed temperature, so that the material in the molecules or atoms of the thermal vibration energy more than the surface binding energy, so that a large number of molecules or atoms evaporate or sublimation, and directly precipitated on the substrate to form a thin film.
Electron beam heating on the use of focused electron beam directly on the bombarded material heating, the kinetic energy of the electron beam into heat energy, so that the material evaporates.
Sputtering technology differs from vacuum evaporation technology.
Most of the particles ejected are in the form of atoms and are often referred to as flowing atoms.
Different sputtering techniques use different types of glow discharges.
