Magnetron sputtering technology is a new type of sputtering technology developed in the 1970s , and has been practically applied in scientific research and production .
2 Principle of Magnetron Sputtering Coating and Magnetron Sputtering Target
The principle of magnetron sputtering coating is to place a magnetron sputtering target in a vacuum chamber , and add sufficient DC voltage between the anode ( vacuum chamber ) and the cathode target ( the material to be deposited ) to form a certain intensity of electrostatic field E .
Under the action of the electrostatic field E , the argon gas ionizes and produces high-energy argon ions A+r and secondary electrons e1 .
On the other hand , when the secondary electron e1 accelerates to the surface of the target , it is subjected to the Lorentz force of the magnetic field B , and makes a circular motion on the surface of the target in the form of a combination of cycloid and helix .
