4 Design Ideas of Cylindrical and Planar Magnetron Sputtering Target
The structure principle of the rectangular plane magnetron target is applied to the cylindrical magnetron sputtering target , and the designed magnetron sputtering target is called the cylindrical and plane magnetron sputtering target .
That is , the uniformity of the coating is good , and the utilization rate of the target is high .
The X axis becomes the axis line , and the magnetic field lines form four closed spaces on the surface of the cylinder , namely the plasma region that restricts the movement of the secondary electron e1 .
In the process of evolving the rectangular planar target into a cylindrical and planar target , the magnets arranged along the X axis in the rectangular planar target become magnets distributed along the axis in the cylindrical and planar target .
Therefore , designing cylindrical and planar magnetron sputtering targets to solve the magnetic field problem at both ends is the key to success .
The magnetic field lines emitted from the outer surface of the “ pole shoe ” are exactly the same direction as the desired ideal ring magnet .
As the target material is consumed , a ring-shaped corrosion pit corresponding to the glow area is formed on the target surface .
As the target material is consumed , a ring corresponding to the glow zone will be formed on the target surface Shaped corrosion pits .
The ground is sputtered away without pits .
When the target material is a precious metal material , this is undoubtedly of great significance .
By adopting the principle of magnets and shoes in the coaxial cylindrical magnetron sputtering target to solve the problem of the end magnetic field , the rectangular planar target can be evolved into a cylindrical and planar magnetron sputtering target .
