The traditional arc ion plating is to apply a DC negative bias on the substrate table to control the ion bombardment energy .
In the DC bias arc ion plating process , in order to suppress the excessive temperature of the substrate caused by the continuous bombardment of the ions on the surface of the substrate , the main measures are to reduce the deposition power , shorten the deposition time , and adopt the intermittent deposition method to reduce the deposition temperature .
Although this method can reduce the deposition temperature , it also reduces some properties of the film , and at the same time reduces the production efficiency and the stability of the film quality .
. In the pulse bias arc ion plating process , since the ions bombard the surface of the substrate in a discontinuous pulse manner , by adjusting the duty cycle of the pulse bias , the temperature gradient between the interior of the substrate and the surface can be changed , thereby changing the internal and the surface of the substrate .
Reduce the total heating effect of ion bombardment to lower the deposition temperature .
