The advantage is that the target material impurity content ( especially gas impurity content ) is low , high density , can be large-scale ; disadvantage is that the melting point and density difference between two or more metals , ordinary melting method is difficult to obtain uniform composition of alloy targets .
Will be a certain ratio of alloy raw materials melting , casting into ingots and then crushed , the crushed powder formed by isostatic pressing , and then high-temperature sintering , the final formation of the target , the advantage is that the target material composition is uniform .
The raw material for copper refining is copper ore , copper ore can be divided into three categories .
Crude copper fire method refining , direct production of copper containing 99.5% to crude copper fire refining , direct production of copper containing more than 99.5% of refined copper .
Crude copper is first refined by fire to remove some impurities , pouring crude copper is first refined by fire to remove some impurities , cast into anodes , and then electrolytic refining , the output contains more than 99.95% copper , the impurity content of the standard refined copper genus .
