The physical properties of metal materials are related to characteristics such as melting point , electrical conductivity , thermal conductivity , density , corrosion resistance , magnetic properties , etc. .
The coefficient of thermal expansion refers to the ratio of the length of the metal to the original length when the temperature of the metal rises by 1℃..For example , in the welding and binding process of the target material , the workpiece to be welded will have uneven thermal expansion due to uneven heating , which will cause the deformation and welding stress of the weldment. .
It is necessary to consider the problem of magnetic field shielding and increase the permeability as much as possible to meet the requirements of sputtering.
. ● Oxidation resistance refers to the ability of metal materials to resist the corrosive effect of oxidizing atmosphere at high temperature .
● Strength : the ability of the material to resist deformation and fracture under external force ( load ). Material per unit area under load is called stress .
● The tensile strength ( σb ) is also called the strength limit , which refers to the maximum stress that the material can withstand before it breaks..The unit is expressed in Newton/mm2 ( N/mm2 ). For example , the tensile strength of aluminum-lithium alloy can reach 689.5MPa .
under static load at room temperature ; materials with δ≤5% are called brittle materials , such as cast iron under static load at room temperature , Glass , ceramics , etc. .
The commonly used hardness is measured according to its range of distribution hardness ( HBS , HBW ), Rockwell hardness ( HRA , HRB , HRC ) and Vickers hardness ( HV ). Brinell hardness and Rockwell hardness are commonly used in production , and the Vickers hardness test is used to determine the hardness of the microstructure .
