So in the preparation process of sputtering alloy target , its method is very important , so what are the common sputtering alloy target preparation methods ?
Special melting method is to melt a certain ratio of alloy raw materials , and then pour the alloy solution in the mold , forming ingots , and then after mechanical processing made of target , casting method in the vacuum melting , casting .
The advantage is that the target impurity content , especially the low content of gas impurities , high density , can be large-scale ; but the disadvantage is that the melting point and density difference between two or more metals , ordinary melting method is difficult to obtain uniform composition of alloy targets , such as titanium aluminum alloy . Second , the powder metallurgy method
The advantage of this method is the target material composition is uniform ; but the disadvantage is low density , high impurity content , commonly used powder metallurgy processes include cold pressing , vacuum hot pressing and hot isostatic pressing .
Strong current heating method using devices that can obtain high current , the use of high current to make the two raw materials of the powder heat , and then apply pressure , so that the two metals themselves react to form an alloy target , this method can be used with the production of titanium-aluminum alloy targets .
The technology has high process efficiency and is suitable for industrial production .
The process is to make the titanium-aluminum powder sintered and shaped under the joint action of heat and force , and take advantage of the low melting point of aluminum in the Ti - AI mixture to bond the titanium powder together to form the sputtering alloy target .
