The operating temperature of diesel generator set is one of the important factors affecting wear and tear.In the process of operation, due to the limitation of cooling system structure, the change of work load and speed, the change of environmental temperature and other factors, the diesel generator set operating temperature has a wide range of variation.Practice shows that the temperature of cooling water is controlled at 75 ~ 85℃ and the temperature of lubricating oil is 75 ~ 95℃.
When the temperature is high, the engine is easy to overheat, low oil viscosity, the wear of parts will increase.When the temperature is low, the viscosity of lubricating oil increases, which makes it difficult for diesel generators to start and operate, and the cooling water cannot keep the normal temperature during operation, which increases the wear and corrosion of parts.The wear of diesel generator set is more serious when starting at low temperature.
