Biodegradable plastics are a type of polymer materials that are degraded through the action of microorganisms that exist in nature, such as molds (fungi), bacteria and algae. Biodegradable plastics not only have excellent degradation properties and can adjust their chemical structure to achieve controllable degradation, and biodegradable plastics have good biocompatibility, thermal stability and mechanical properties, and they also have relatively stable chemical properties.
