Chemical modification is the combination of active groups or monomers with biodegradable plastics in the form of covalent bonds, which can be specifically divided into copolymerization modification, chain extension modification, graft modification and crosslinking modification. Chemical modification can strengthen the toughness of the material, improve the mechanical properties and processing performance, and also reduce the production cost.
Cross-linking modification: Under the influence of some external factors, the polymer macromolecular chain generates reactive free radicals or functional groups, thereby forming new chemical bonds between the macromolecular chains, making the linear structure polymer shape
