On the bag making machine, the heat sealing temperature is directly displayed by the thermometer, the heat sealing time can be indirectly calculated by means of the bag making speed and heat sealing ratio, and the heat sealing pressure is mainly evaluated by the operator’s experience.
Under the premise of constant pressure, when the bag-making processing speed is increased, the heat sealing temperature must be increased accordingly.
In other words, accelerating the bag making speed will shorten the heat sealing time, increasing the heat sealing ratio will extend the heat sealing time, and increasing the “gap” will increase the heat sealing pressure and extend the heat sealing time at the same time.
As a basic principle, only the resin of the heat seal layer should be melted during the bag making process, and the resin of the composite layer should not be melted!
If the heat-sealing pressure is appropriate but the heat-sealing temperature is too low, or the heat-sealing pressure is insufficient and the heat-sealing temperature is too low, although the appearance of the bag will be flat and the separation of the composite film will also occur between the heat covers, it will appear “The heat seal is not secure” problem.
If the heat-sealing pressure (to varying degrees) is low and the heat-sealing temperature is too high (when the heat-sealing pressure is low, the heat-sealing temperature must rise accordingly!
