All the news related to the latest Microsoft operating system, Windows 11.
Despite the fact that its release to the market was quite bumpy, it seems that Windows 11 has finally found…
As you probably already know, some time ago Windows 11 was officially presented, the new version of Microsoft's operating system that can now be downloaded and installed easily. Windows 10 users can upgrade to Windows XNUMX for free, keeping at all times the data and information saved on the computer.
1.3 Downloading and installing Windows 11 on your computer
As we mentioned, updating to Windows 11 is possible on any computer that currently run Windows 10 and comply with minimum installation requirements of the new system, where the following is specified:
System firmware: UEFI, Supports Secure Boot.
In the event that your computer complies with them, you can continue with the installation of Windows 11 on it. Now, it is important that you know that you must have an active internet connection at all times to avoid potential problems during installation.
To begin, you will download the Windows 11 Setup Wizard, available for free at the Microsoft download page. To do this, you just have to press on the blue button called «Download now» and a small wizard will be downloaded to help you through the Windows 11 download and installation process.
To do this, all you have to do is follow the link that the window itself shows To access Microsoft's PC Health download page y click on the button «Download the PC Status Check app», a tool that you must install on your computer.
We show you all the models that will be compatible with Windows 11
Once it has been officially verified that the computer meets the minimum requirements necessary to install Windows 11 on it, it is time to start with the download and installation. To do this, you must return to the installation program downloaded in the first step, and click on the "Update" button so you can collect the data from the equipment check tool.
Windows 11 is now official: this is Microsoft's new operating system
Windows 11 includes a large number of security features (such as the TPM 2.0 chip requirement), features designed to help make computers even more protected from cyber attacks such as ramsonware. But Which is better?
It is increasingly common to see news related to ransomware attacks, attacks that encrypt all content in exchange for a ransom. Thanks to the TPM chip that Microsoft had not taken advantage of until now, this type of attack has its days numbered.
11 If you can't update, no problem
The most important novelty visually striking, we find it in the design. Since Windows 3.11, Microsoft always it offered us the start button on the left side bottom of the taskbar.
Microsoft, however, has been given that in a 16: 9 monitor (the most common), placing the start menu in the center is much more comfortable for the user since to interact with it you don't have to turn your head.
In addition, it has also launched different applications to be able to manage the smartphone from our PC (You Phone application), without having to interact with it at any time, very similar to the integration that we find between iOS and macOS, but on Android.
In Windows 11, this functionality is increased with the possibility of modify the width of each of the applications.
La desktop management in Windows 10 It has never been the best, in fact it left a lot to be desired for all of us who work with several desktops where we have different applications open.
Snap Groups allows us assign apps to desktops, desks that have memory and when we open them they know on which desk they have to be placed.
Widgets are back
Icon and typography redesign It was a matter of time before Microsoft the font will change so much used in Windows as the design of the icons, icons that had the same design for more than 20 years.
More touchscreen support Although Windows 10 does not work badly with touchscreen devices, had a lot of room for improvement.
Microsoft has changed the update cycle with Windows 11 and will only release one big update per year, just as Apple does with the Mac operating system. In this way, users will be more tempted to upgrade to see the new improvements that are added.
If your computer is not compatible with Windows 11, there is no problem, you do not need to start saving (although you should) to buy a new computer, since you have until 2025.
