Yoga is not just asanas – the practice of body postures.It is a way of accessing our infinite possibilities and powers.
But who is listening to these words now?According to yogic philosophy, that silent observer and listener of your thoughts is your consciousness.
Consciousness is said to be light emanating from within the body.Some call it our soul or higher self.Meditation is a tool we can use to gain better access to our higher self – our soul self (atman), also known as our pure state of consciousness.
After we understand that atman transcends mind and body, we can test this theory by pratyahara (ie cutting off our senses).For example, when we restrict our senses by closing our eyes or blocking our hearing, we are literally starving the brain of information.
Even 10 minutes a day in samadhi can be very beneficial for mental health.We live in a world that tells us that our worth is equal to our productivity.This constant state of doing things can drain us and leave us feeling disconnected from our true selves.
This state is how we make decisions based on love, logic, and patience, rather than from our heads, which are generated by impatience or fleeting emotions that often distort our judge.
